CycloneDX SBOM Generator
Copyright 2026 Odinex

This product includes software and data from third parties, used at run time:

1. Syft -- Copyright Anchore, Inc. (Apache License 2.0)
   https://github.com/anchore/syft
   Downloaded and installed at run time from the official Anchore releases;
   generates the CycloneDX SBOM from lockfiles. Not bundled in this repository.

2. OSV.dev -- operated by Google. https://osv.dev
   Package purls from the generated SBOM are sent to the OSV API
   (https://api.osv.dev) for vulnerability matching. Advisory content is
   authored by the OSV ecosystem and is surfaced with its own identifiers
   (CVE, GHSA, PYSEC, ...).

3. Exploit Prediction Scoring System (EPSS) -- Forum of Incident Response
   and Security Teams (FIRST). https://www.first.org
   CVE identifiers are sent to the FIRST EPSS API to retrieve exploit
   probability scores.

4. Known Exploited Vulnerabilities (KEV) catalog -- Cybersecurity and
   Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA), U.S. Department of Homeland Security.
   The public KEV JSON feed is downloaded once per run. No data is sent to CISA.

